  "applicability_scope": [
    "User-reported Level 1 review of the two Published theorem statements and relevant definitions; dependency tracking does not independently audit every dependency.",
    "Theorem 3.3: representative uniform generation iff bounded group-closure witness cardinalities, on a nonempty countable domain with a UUS class, countable partition, and positive tolerance.",
    "Theorem 3.7: representative nonuniform generation iff an increasing uniform cover at each positive tolerance. The public statement omits the source's countability, UUS, and partition assumptions; groups may overlap or fail to cover the arbitrary domain. Covers may depend on tolerance.",
    "Semantic randomized finite-history generators; distinct-sample empirical proportions; supremum distance; representativeness at every positive history length; probability-one freshness and target membership after the threshold.",
    "Target-contained streams need not be complete presentations. Uniform thresholds precede all targets and streams; nonuniform thresholds may depend on the target but not its stream.",
    "Bounded-witness group-closure finiteness, rather than a claim of literal numerical zero/infinity conventions or optimal sample complexity."
  ],
